== 3.7 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The rate of heat flow through a rod of thermal conductivity $k$, area $A$ and length $L$, whose ends differ by $theta$, is],
  [$k theta \/ (A L)$],
  [$k L \/ (A theta)$],
  [$k A L \/ theta$],
  [$k A theta \/ L$]
)

#mcq(2, [The SI unit of thermal conductivity is],
  [W m⁻¹ K⁻¹],
  [W K⁻¹],
  [J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹],
  [W m⁻² K⁻¹]
)

#mcq(3, [Which of these materials is the best thermal conductor?],
  [glass],
  [copper],
  [wood],
  [air]
)

#mcq(4, [Metals conduct heat better than non-metals because],
  [they are denser],
  [they contain free electrons that carry energy quickly],
  [their atoms are heavier],
  [they melt at lower temperatures]
)

#mcq(5, [A rod of length 0.50 m and area $2.0 times 10^(-4)$ m² carries heat between ends at 100 °C and 20 °C. If $k = 400$ W m⁻¹ K⁻¹, the rate of flow is],
  [1.3 W],
  [128 W],
  [1.28 kW],
  [12.8 W]
)

#mcq(6, [A glass window of area 1.0 m² and thickness 4.0 mm has inside 20 °C and outside 5 °C. If $k = 0.8$ W m⁻¹ K⁻¹, the heat lost per second is],
  [300 W],
  [30 000 W],
  [3000 W],
  [30 W]
)

#mcq(7, [Trapped air is a good insulator because],
  [air is a poor conductor and, when trapped, cannot carry a convection current],
  [air has a high thermal conductivity],
  [air radiates strongly],
  [air is a metal vapour]
)

#mcq(8, [Double glazing reduces heat loss mainly by],
  [using thicker glass],
  [reducing the area of the window],
  [trapping a layer of air or gas between two panes],
  [making the glass reflective only]
)

